    "body": "Adds a optional `vim.fs.abspath.Opts` parameter to `vim.fs.abspath`\nwith the following optional fields.\n1. `cwd` option to specify directory akin to `--relative-from` in\n`realpath(1)`.\n2. `plain` option to disable expansion of tilde (~) in paths.\n\n## Problem\nNeovim has no facilities for resolving paths that are relative to\nother arbritrary paths. Implementing the logic manually is error-prone\non Windows specifically due to path magic and makes writing a portable\nsolution needlessly involved.\nThe above functionality is also needed without unwarranted tilde expansion,\nwhich may corrupt valid paths that never went through a shell.\n\n## Solution\nThis commit adds support for specifying a current working directory\nfrom which a directory agnostic path may be obtained. It also\nprovides support for specifying plain paths which are not to be\nexpanded.\n",
